.TH AUSPEX 1 "October 2026" "Auspex 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
auspex \- the Auspex interpreter (a lightweight PL/SQL-style scripting language)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B auspex
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Auspex compiles C-like source files (\fI*.apx\fR) to bytecode for a small
stack VM and can run against either its built-in custom SQL engine or an
optional SQLite backend. Without a file argument, an interactive REPL is
started.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-DNAME
Define a conditional-compilation flag (repeatable). Applies to the input
file and its imports; use with \fB$if NAME $then ... $end\fR directives.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " PATH"
Open a SQLite database (\fI:memory:\fR allowed) instead of the built-in
custom engine. Disabled in builds with \fBUSE_SQLITE=0\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short usage summary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH REPL
When started without a file, Auspex reads statements interactively.
Dot-commands include \fB.exit\fR/\fB.quit\fR, \fB.help\fR, \fB.load\fR,
\fB.connect\fR, \fB.tables\fR, \fB.schema\fR, \fB.columns\fR,
\fB.count\fR, \fB.sql\fR, \fB.vars\fR, \fB.defs\fR, and \fB.history\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I auspex.db
Default database file for the custom engine. If it is missing and a
MyPL-era \fImypl.db\fR exists, that file is used instead (with a warning).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run a program against the custom engine:
.B auspex program.apx
.TP
Run against an in-memory SQLite database with a debug flag:
.B auspex -DDEBUG program.apx --db :memory:
.SH SEE ALSO
The documentation in docs/ (language.md, engines.md, examples.md), the
README, and the examples/ directory in the source distribution.
